<title>GERMANY: Waigel - chance of trade tax compromise good in 98.</title>
<headline>Waigel - chance of trade tax compromise good in 98.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Finance Minister Theo Waigel said on Friday that there was a good chance of reaching a compromise on abolishing the trade tax on capital in 1998.</p>
<p>&quot;The chances for a compromise on the scrapping of trade tax on capital next year are relatively good,&quot; Waigel said in a speech at a banking seminar.</p>
<p>--Catherine O'Mahony, Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
